@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Deploy Planner
  "Diffs local build_dir against remote deploy path using rsync dry-run and returns plan counts."

  Provides:
    - deploy.Runner @source("symbol:Runner")
    - deploy.Planner @source("symbol:Planner")
    - deploy.NewPlanner @source("symbol:NewPlanner")
    - deploy.Plan @source("symbol:Plan")
    - deploy.PlanOptions @source("symbol:PlanOptions")
    - deploy.Planner.Plan
    - deploy.ParseCompareOutput @source("symbol:ParseCompareOutput")

  Consumes:
    - config.Target
    - remote.CompareDryRunRequest
    - remote.RsyncDestinationFromTarget

  Invariants:
    - Plan MUST require deploy.build_dir and deploy.remote_path on the target
    - Plan MUST run rsync with dry-run, itemize-changes, and stats only — no bytes transferred
    - ParseCompareOutput MUST derive new, changed, unchanged, remove, and bytes-to-send from rsync stats

  OutOfScope:
    - Running deploy transfers (future M-061)
    - CLI commands for deploy and status (future M-061)
    - Share object store or manifest interaction

  Scenario (happy-path): Plan with changes
    Given local build_dir differs from remote
    When Plan runs
    Then counts and bytes-to-send reflect rsync dry-run stats

  Scenario (happy-path): Already up to date
    Given local build_dir matches remote
    When Plan runs
    Then transferred counts are zero and unchanged equals local file count

  Scenario (negative): Missing deploy config
    Given a target without build_dir or remote_path
    When Plan runs
    Then it returns a validation error before rsync
